Declarative transport for a Roland REAC (EtherType 0x8819) stream across an
OpenWrt network: a gretap tunnel, its 8021q VLAN sub-interfaces and br-lan
membership, and an fw4-sourced Layer-2 return-path drop — all expressed as
native netifd (UCI) and firewall4 config. No compiled code: the package ships
only nftables/UCI config and uci-defaults shims that merge the fabric into the
box's own network at install.

## Third-party code and references

This package embeds no third-party code. It is an original configuration layer
over standard OpenWrt subsystems (netifd / gretap, the 8021q bridge VLAN filter,
and firewall4 / nftables).

REAC's EtherType (0x8819) is referenced only as an interoperability datum — the
fabric carries REAC frames but does not parse them. Interface facts of this kind
are not copyrightable; no third-party code is copied and no third-party copyright
attaches.
